=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  status apparmor-logging --------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Debian 13, as the engine's scenarios start from it: sshd on 22$
# through ssh.service, ufw active allowing 22, alice in sudo, no$
# unattended-upgrades; up 3 days. AppArmor's profiles are in$
# complain mode.$
$
hardn  v0.4.0              https://github.com/abbott/hardn$
$
# Debian 13 (Trixie) ###########################################$
$
  [web-01]                 192.0.2.20$
                           3 days, 5 hours, 12 minutes$
$
  [*] Risk Level           High ~ weak security$
$
  [+] User                 + non-root, sudo$
  [ ] SSH                  Not Configured password auth on$
                             ~ Default port (22)$
  [+] Firewall             + deny policy$
  [ ] Kernel               Not Configured 5 to set$
  [ ] Auto Updates         Not Configured no unattended-upgrades$
  [ ] AppArmor             Partial logging only$
$
----------------------------------------------------------------$
$
  Select an option         Mode Live$
$
   1) User                 Create, manage (sudo, SSH keys)$
   2) SSH                  Disable root and passwords, set port$
   3) Firewall             Manage rules, port listening$
   4) Kernel               Harden sysctl (network, kernel)$
   6) Run All              Queue hardening actions$
   7) Backup               Configure hardn backup$
   8) Configuration        hardn.yml, dns, ntp, syslog$
   9) System Details       View system info$
  10) Logs                 View hardn logs$
$
   0) Exit                 q to quit$
$
    > Option [0-4, 6-10 or q]:$
$
$

